      "id": "P1",
      "text": "COLONOSCOPY AND THERAPEUTIC ENDOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 8, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: A. Synthetic, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Procedure: Colonoscopy with balloon dilation and polypectomy"
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "The patient has ileocolonic Crohn disease and underwent an ileocecal resection in 2017."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "A colonoscopy from January 2024 described a narrowed anastomosis and a 4 mm rectal polyp that was removed at that earlier encounter."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "No dilation was carried out in 2024."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "The colonoscope was introduced through the anus and advanced to the ileocolonic anastomosis."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "Ileocolonic anastomosis and balloon dilation"
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "A short anastomotic stricture was present."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "A through-the-scope balloon was advanced across the stricture and inflated to 15 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "The colonoscope then traversed the treated narrowing into the neo-terminal ileum."
    },
    {
      "id": "P13",
      "text": "Descending colon: cold-snare polypectomy"
    },
    {
      "id": "P14",
      "text": "A 9 mm sessile polyp in the descending colon was removed with a cold snare and retrieved."
    },
    {
      "id": "P15",
      "text": "Surveillance colonoscopy in 3 years."
    }
  ],
